   "final_message": "All 6 sweep points are clean \u2014 DRC 0 and LVS match at every point.\n\nFinal status: `/inv.icl` is complete and verified. The layout follows the `l1_param_inv.icl` pattern adapted for the inverter's fixed netlist (nmos drain=VGND/source=Y, pmos drain=VPWR/source=Y). Key design decisions:\n\n- **Y strap on the right** (drain columns `dnl`/`dpl` labelled `net=Y`), supplies on the left, so the gate contact can be placed `left_of=y` with `xspace=0.17` \u2014 avoiding the li.3/li.c2 spacing violations between the gate-contact li and the output strap (lesson 11).\n- **Gate contact** uses `cb = max(nd.top + 0.19, snl.top + 0.25, dnl.top + 0.25)` (n-row only, per lesson 1), `enclose gc poly by=minx`, `enclose gc npc`, and `enclose gc li net=A` for the input pin.\n- **Diffusion width** `w=(L + 0.53)` derives from L so it follows the sweep; `width=3` columns (1.38 \u00b5m) fits even at L=0.25.\n- **Ports** on met1-enclosed li shapes (`ap`, `yp`) for pin access.\n\nThe hard part was the gate-contact/output-strap spacing conflict \u2014 resolved by putting Y on the drain side and shifting the gate contact left of the Y strap.",
