   "final_message": "All checks pass. Here's the final summary:\n\n**Status: CLEAN** \u2014 `/nand2.icl` passes DRC + LVS at the nominal point and all 6 sweep points.\n\n**What was hard:** The main challenge was getting the gate-contact placement right. The initial version had `cb` (gate-contact bottom) computed using `myl.top` (the p-row Y contact), which pushed the gate contacts up into the n-tap row, causing licon.14/licon.9/licon.7 violations and poly.2 shorts. Removing `myl.top` from the `cb` max() fixed this \u2014 gate contacts belong in the empty band between the n and p diffusions, not near the tap rows.\n\n**Key design decisions:**\n- Gate order A\u2192B on both n and p rows (same order required by lesson 10)\n- n-row: Y contact at left end, VGND at right end; n1 is a series node with no contact between gates\n- p-row: VPWR at both ends, Y contact in the middle (shared between parallel devices)\n- Output Y doesn't line up between rows (n-side left end vs p-side middle), so `route Y layers=m1,m2` joins them\n- Gate contacts shifted outward (\u00b10.1) to avoid clashing with supply straps\n- `width=4` columns (1.84 \u00b5m) fits even at L=0.25",
