   "final_message": "All 6 sweep points are clean \u2014 DRC 0, LVS match at every point.\n\n**Final status:** `/nor2.icl` is complete and clean at the nominal point and across the full sweep (L=0.18/0.25, widths \u00d70.85/\u00d71.35/\u00d71.9, H up to 4.08).\n\n**What was hard:** The NOR2 topology has parallel n-devices (A, B both pull Y to VGND) and series p-devices (A then B from VPWR through n1 to Y), so the gate order A\u2192B must match in both rows while the diffusion islands differ (n-row: VGND|A|Y|B|VGND with Y in the middle; p-row: VPWR|A|n1|B|Y with n1 as a contactless series node and Y at the right end). Key challenges resolved:\n- **Gate pitch \u2265 0.54 \u00b5m** so the two poly gate pads (0.33 wide) clear each other, using `left=(ga.right + max(0.28, 0.54 - L))` which scales with L.\n- **Gate contacts pushed outward** (A left, B right) so the pads don't short neighboring poly (poly.2 rule), with n-row items only in `cb` per lesson 1.\n- **Y output not aligned** between n-row (middle contact) and p-row (right-end contact), so `route Y layers=m1,m2` joins them instead of a strap near a gate (avoiding li.3 and SHORT X/n1).\n- **`width=5` columns** (2.3 \u00b5m) chosen so the diffusion fits at L=0.25 with the wider gate pitch.",
