   "final_message": "All 6 sweep points are clean \u2014 DRC 0, LVS match at every point.\n\n**Final status:** `/nand3.icl` is complete and verified clean across the full sweep.\n\n**What was hard:** The main challenge was getting the gate pitch right. The poly gate-contact pads (0.33 \u00b5m wide) need 0.21 \u00b5m between them, so neighbouring gates need a centre-to-centre pitch of at least 0.54 \u00b5m. My first attempt used a gap of 0.28 \u00b5m between gates, which put the contact pads only 0.09 \u00b5m apart (violating poly.2). I had to increase the inter-gate gap to 0.60 \u00b5m (pitch = L + 0.60 = 0.75 \u00b5m at nominal) so the pads clear. The rest followed the established NAND2/inverter pattern: shared diffusion islands with series n-stack (A\u2192n2\u2192B\u2192n1\u2192C\u2192VGND) and parallel p-devices (all VPWR\u2192Y), gate contacts placed at gate.cx with cb derived only from n-row items, output Y joined via `route Y layers=m1` since n-side and p-side drains don't line up, and ports on met1.",
