   "final_message": "All 6 sweep points are clean \u2014 DRC 0, LVS match at every point.\n\n## Summary\n\nBuilt `/and2.icl` \u2014 a parametric standard cell for `and2` (NAND2 + inverter) in SKY130.\n\n**Key design decisions:**\n- **Gate order A, B, n1** shared identically across both n and p rows, enabling full diffusion sharing with no island breaks.\n- **Diffusion columns**: n-row = n1 | n2 | VGND | X; p-row = VPWR | n1 | VPWR | X \u2014 each column derived from `L` and fixed gaps so it scales across the sweep.\n- **Gate pitch** `gap = max(0.28, 0.74 - L)` keeps poly contact pads \u2265 0.21 apart even at L=0.25.\n- **Gate contacts** all bottom-aligned by n-row only (`cb = max(nd.top + 0.19, ...)`), with the n1 contact shifted left by 0.13 away from the output strap (avoiding li.3 violations).\n- **n1 net** (internal): n-row col0 and p-row col1 don't line up, so `route n1 layers=m2` joins them, with an mcon+met1 access point.\n- **Output X**: n and p drains line up at the rightmost column, joined by a vertical li strap; pin placed on met1 at diffusion-row height (not gate-contact height).\n- **width=8 columns** (3.68 \u00b5m) fits comfortably at L=0.25.\n\nThe hardest part was balancing the gate contact placement \u2014 shifting the n1 contact away from the output strap while keeping all three contacts on their gates and maintaining 0.21 pad spacing \u2014 plus ensuring the internal n1 route had a legal met1 access point without colliding with the B input pin.",
